The code statements that lead to the bug are:
```c
// Missing clock references for UFS MEM and UFS CARD controllers
// No definitions for gcc_ufs_card_clkref_en and gcc_ufs_mem_clkref_en
```
Reason:
The absence of the necessary clock references for the UFS MEM and UFS CARD controllers in the clock management system resulted in improper clock signal management, which likely affected the functionality of these controllers.

The code statements that fix the bug are:
```c
static struct clk_branch gcc_ufs_card_clkref_en = {
	.halt_reg = 0x8c004,
	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT,
	.clkr = {
		.enable_reg = 0x8c004,
		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
			.name = "gcc_ufs_card_clkref_en",
			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
		},
	},
};

static struct clk_branch gcc_ufs_mem_clkref_en = {
	.halt_reg = 0x8c000,
	.halt_check = BRANCH_HALT,
	.clkr = {
		.enable_reg = 0x8c000,
		.enable_mask = BIT(0),
		.hw.init = &(const struct clk_init_data) {
			.name = "gcc_ufs_mem_clkref_en",
			.ops = &clk_branch2_ops,
		},
	},
};
```
Reason:
The addition of the `gcc_ufs_card_clkref_en` and `gcc_ufs_mem_clkref_en` structures provides the necessary clock references for the UFS MEM and UFS CARD controllers, ensuring proper clock signal management and restoring the functionality of these controllers.

